Bring enough /WoDeath charges and air elementals are just a minor
issue.

> Once I neglected to fireproof my gloves,
> they burned up and I hit a cockatrice

Impossible.  Fire damage to armor will never completely destroy gloves,
although lava can destroy your boots.  The things that could make you
lose/remove your gloves would be:
1) Seduction
2) nymph theft
3) Self-polymorph
4) Destroy armor spell/scroll
5) Taking your armor off using the "T" command or the "A" command.

> Starved a number of times

Carry a few K-rations.  Wear a "AoLS.  Pre-stuff yourself with an
entire dragon corpse before leaving the dungeon.

> Once I tried to zap a /odeath and changed my mind by hitting ".".
> I don't know what happened to my "oreflection.

Reflection never helps when you zap a wand in direction "."

> Once my unicorn horn got cursed and
> I kept trying to un-confuse-stun myself and died.

Check your inventory EVERY time before applying a unicorn horn.
If the horn becomes unblessed, bless it before you need to use it
again.

With stats and intrinsics like you've posted, here is a list of the
things that can still kill you:

1) Stoning
2) Dissolving in lava
3) Sickness.
4) Decapitation.
5) Self-genocide / Zapping /WoDeath or casting FoD at "."
6) Trying to eat a rider.
7) Summoning storm filling the entire level with Archons.

If you are worried about any of these things, wear an "oLS.

All of these are non-hitpoint related.  With an armor class of -128,
even the riders should almost never be able to land a hit on you.

To protect against lava, which is the only thing you know you WILL have
to face, you can:
1) switch your speed boots with fireproof water walking boots.
2) Carry a few wands of cold, and break one if you fall in lava.
3) Levitate the whole time, from the Plane of Air until you arrive at
astral.
4) Know the spell of "cone of cold" and be ready to cast it at
yourself.

The things that CAN'T kill you anymore are:
1) Drowning/choking (You can survive without air)
2) Swallowed digestion (You have slower digestion)

There are also the two major and one minor things to avoid:
1) Remember to check that you have the real "AoY before you climb the
stairs on dlvl 1
2) Make sure you don't sacrifice the amulet on the wrong altar.

3) Do not levelport to a dungeon level less than 1.

Your biggest worry should be that your stuff can get lost/cursed,
leaving you with no way to reach the altar. So you should keep a backup
sack in your main inventory with vital items like wands of teleport and
death, a couple of blessed potions of full healing, and an emergency
wish or two.  And do NOT wield a two-handed weapon, EVER.

And it would make a LOT of sense to fix up your luck and prayer status
before you enter the planes.


